# AC 4  - a one-shot at a named time: scheduled once, with the time said back.
# AC 5  - it comes back with an identifier you can read.
# AC 14 - the listing: identifier, schedule, prompt, whether it repeats, next run.
#
# 14:30 is far enough out that it cannot fire during the run and muddy the
# listing. Whether the model turns "14:30 today" into `30 14 * * *` and sets
# repeating false is its aim, and that is part of what this row tests.

wait: 8
send: Schedule a one-off prompt for 14:30 today that says exactly: hello. It must run once only and must never repeat.
wait: 190
mark: === AC 4 and AC 5 above: scheduled once, 14:30 said back, an identifier to read ===

send: List everything that is scheduled right now.
idle: 200
mark: === AC 14 above: identifier, schedule, prompt, repeats or not, next run ===

send: /exit
